{"term":"assumption","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:ec5f6b9d70755d92b7","definition":"The act of assuming, or taking to or upon oneself; the act of taking up or adopting.","example":"His assumption of secretarial duties was timely.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["assumption of risk","Assumption Parish","deed of assumption","heroic assumption","misassumption","non-assumption","nonassumption","preassumption","reassumption","self-assumption","subassumption"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assumption#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:acf3a1eb4ca7735ce1","definition":"The act of taking for granted, or supposing a thing without proof; a supposition; an unwarrantable claim.","example":"Their assumption of his guilt disqualified them from jury duty.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["assumption of risk","Assumption Parish","deed of assumption","heroic assumption","misassumption","non-assumption","nonassumption","preassumption","reassumption","self-assumption","subassumption"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assumption#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e2106bb18d52f5bd0e","definition":"The thing supposed; a postulate, or proposition assumed; a supposition.","example":"No doubt a finite evaluative argument must make some unargued evaluative assumptions, just as finite factual arguments must make some unargued factual assumptions.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["assumption of risk","Assumption Parish","deed of assumption","heroic assumption","misassumption","non-assumption","nonassumpt